{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Hecke.Algebra","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Hecke.Algebra","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.Hecke.Generators","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Algebra.Defs","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Algebra.Subalgebra.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.RingTheory.Adjoin.Basic"],"declarations":9,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Hecke.HeckeAlgebra.inv_formula","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Hecke.HeckeAlgebra.inv_formula","kind":"theorem","line":74,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Hecke/Algebra.lean#L74-L90","doc":"The inverse of σ_i is σ_i - (q - q⁻¹), derivable from the Hecke\nquadratic relation: σ_i · (σ_i - (q - q⁻¹)) = σ_i² - (q-q⁻¹)σ_i = 1. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Hecke.HeckeAlgebra.gen","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Hecke.HeckeAlgebra.gen","kind":"def","line":69,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Hecke/Algebra.lean#L69-L72","doc":"The image of generator `i` in the algebra. Convenience alias for\n`HeckeAlgebra.embed i`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Hecke.HeckeAlgebra.spans","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Hecke.HeckeAlgebra.spans","kind":"theorem","line":62,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Hecke/Algebra.lean#L62-L62","doc":"Spanning property: `A` is generated as an `R`-algebra by the\nimage of `embed`. Captured via `Algebra.adjoin` for compatibility\nwith Mathlib's subalgebra API. Without this field the typeclass\nwould admit any algebra containing the generators rather than the\nHecke quotient itself. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Hecke.HeckeAlgebra.farCommute","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Hecke.HeckeAlgebra.farCommute","kind":"theorem","line":56,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Hecke/Algebra.lean#L56-L56","doc":"Far-commutativity: σ_i σ_j = σ_j σ_i for |i - j| ≥ 2. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Hecke.HeckeAlgebra.braid","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Hecke.HeckeAlgebra.braid","kind":"theorem","line":54,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Hecke/Algebra.lean#L54-L54","doc":"Braid relation: σ_i σ_{i+1} σ_i = σ_{i+1} σ_i σ_{i+1}. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Hecke.HeckeAlgebra.quadratic","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Hecke.HeckeAlgebra.quadratic","kind":"theorem","line":52,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Hecke/Algebra.lean#L52-L52","doc":"Hecke quadratic relation: σ_i² = (q - q⁻¹)σ_i + 1. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Hecke.HeckeAlgebra.embed","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Hecke.HeckeAlgebra.embed","kind":"def","line":50,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Hecke/Algebra.lean#L50-L50","doc":"The generator embedding σ_i ↦ embed i. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Hecke.HeckeAlgebra.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Hecke.HeckeAlgebra.mk","kind":"ctor","line":47,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Hecke/Algebra.lean#L47-L47","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Hecke.HeckeAlgebra","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Hecke.HeckeAlgebra","kind":"class","line":36,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Hecke/Algebra.lean#L36-L62","doc":"The Iwahori–Hecke algebra `H_n(q)` over `R`, axiomatised as a\ntypeclass. An instance asserts: an `R`-algebra `A` with a chosen\ngenerator embedding `embed : Generator n → A` satisfying the three\nHecke relations.\n\nThe `spans` field captures that `A` is generated as an `R`-algebra\nby `embed`'s image (every element is a finite `R`-linear combination\nof monomials in the generators). Stated existentially to keep the\nclass lightweight.\n","signatureChunk":0}]}